{"agent":"bugs","findings":[{"id":"bugs-001","file":"triggarr/web/routes.py","line":45,"title":"Reverts fix e11187e: HTML autoescaping (XSS protection) now depends on Starlette's deprecated env_options passthrough","category":"logic-error","cwe":"CWE-79","severity":"medium","agent_confidence":72,"in_diff":true,"intent_doc_match":null,"problem":"This diff undoes the previous commit (e11187e, 'use preconfigured jinja2.Environment for autoescape'). It goes back to passing autoescape=True as an extra keyword through Jinja2Templates(directory=..., **env_options). The installed Starlette (0.52.1, starlette/templating.py:92-96) still accepts that path but marks it deprecated: importing triggarr.web.routes raises 'DeprecationWarning: Extra environment options are deprecated. Use a preconfigured jinja2.Environment instead.' I confirmed this by running the import with -W error::DeprecationWarning. pyproject.toml lists fastapi and jinja2 with no version pin, so whether autoescaping is configured now depends on whatever Starlette version gets installed. The old code set autoescape=True directly on its own jinja2.Environment, so it held on any version. If a later Starlette removes **env_options, the app fails at import with a TypeError (startup abort). If a future version stops honoring the option, templates render user-controlled content unescaped (script injection). Today escaping still works because Starlette's _create_env also defaults autoescape to True, but that is a library default, not this code's guarantee. Any test run with warnings set to errors will also fail.","current_code":"templates = Jinja2Templates(directory=str(TEMPLATES_DIR), autoescape=True)","fix_hint":"restore the preconfigured jinja2.Environment(loader=FileSystemLoader(...), autoescape=True) passed via env=","why_it_matters":"Escaping that prevents XSS should not depend on a deprecated, unpinned framework path. The likeliest outcome is a startup crash after a dependency upgrade.","silenced_marker_nearby":false}],"agent_notes":["Verified: Starlette 0.52.1 installed; Jinja2Templates.__init__ emits a DeprecationWarning when env_options are passed. The commit message of e11187e claims Starlette removed the passthrough; in 0.52.1 it is deprecated, not removed."]}
